# Sunken Hollow: "This land enters tapped unless you control two or more basic lands." Turn 5 Bot1 controls an Island (one
# basic) and an Underground Sea (the Island and Swamp types, but not basic, CR 205.4a): one basic is below the two, so its
# Sunken Hollow enters tapped - though Bot2, its opponent, controls two basic lands by then. Bot2 with an Island and a
# Swamp of its own plays the same land on turn 6 and it enters untapped (positive control).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Underground Sea
Sunken Hollow
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Swamp
Sunken Hollow
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Underground Sea.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Sunken Hollow.Play
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Sunken Hollow.Play

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Sunken Hollow.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Sunken Hollow.Tapped = false
